course: dictionary
lesson: 635
title: Backlog: work still waiting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A backlog is a pile of work or jobs that should have been done already but are still waiting. Context tells you this. «There was a big backlog of cases, a pile of cases waiting to be dealt with.» The words pile and waiting are your clues: the work has not been finished yet.
explain: You will meet backlog at school and in computing too. If you were ill for a week, you might come back with a backlog of homework. In a computer team, the backlog is the list of jobs still to be done, usually put in order. The phrases «a backlog of» and «clear the backlog» are useful to remember.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. "There was a big pile of cases waiting to be dealt with" still makes sense, so backlog means that pile. If a sentence stops making sense, try another meaning or look the word up.
fact: A backlog is a pile of work or jobs that should have been done already and are still waiting.
fact: «Clear the backlog» means finish all the jobs that have been waiting.
fact: A backlog builds up when there is too much work and too little time.
fact: In computing, a backlog is the team's list of jobs to do, often in order.
fact: After being ill, a pupil can have a backlog of homework to catch up on.
exercise: «There was a big backlog of cases, a pile of cases waiting to be dealt with.» What is a backlog? | A type of tree in the park | *A pile of work still waiting to be done | A holiday with lots of fun | A quick, tidy finish
exercise: A pupil was ill for a week and came back to school. Which phrase best shows a backlog? | *A backlog of homework | A cloud of dust | A pair of new shoes | A field of wheat
exercise: The team says, «We must clear the backlog today.» What does clear the backlog mean? | *Finish the jobs that have been waiting | Paint the whole office | Lose the list of jobs | Empty the bin of rubbish
test: In «a backlog of emails waiting to be answered», what does waiting tell you? | The emails are funny | The emails are long | *The emails are still not finished | The emails are already answered
test: A computer team keeps a backlog. What is it? | *A list of jobs still to be done, in order | A machine that cleans the screen | A rule that jobs must be done at night | A list of the team's favourite games
exam: Which sentence uses backlog correctly? | A backlog is a loud noise from the sea | *The team had a backlog of tasks to finish before Friday | The dog had a backlog of bones in the garden | She ate a backlog of cake for tea
